# 必考词 Unit22
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit22核心词汇

{{arise}}{{/əˈraɪz}}{{v. 出现； arise；起身}}{{Problems may arise during the implementation.}}
{{assert}}{{/əˈsɜːt}}{{v. 断言； assert；坚持}}{{He asserted his innocence throughout the trial.}}
{{assess}}{{/əˈses}}{{v. 评估； assess；评定}}{{The damage was assessed by insurance experts.}}
{{assign}}{{/əˈsaɪn}}{{v. 分配； assign；指派}}{{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{assist}}{{/əˈsɪst}}{{v. 帮助； assist；援助}}{{The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation.}}
{{associate}}{{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt}}{{v./n. 联系； associate；同事}}{{People often associate the color red with danger.}}
{{assume}}{{/əˈsjuːm}}{{v. 假设； assume；承担}}{{I assume you have read the instructions.}}
{{assure}}{{/əˈʃʊər}}{{v. 保证； assure；使确信}}{{I assure you that the product is safe.}}
{{attach}}{{/əˈtætʃ}}{{v. 附上； attach；依恋}}{{Please attach your resume to the email.}}
{{attain}}{{/əˈteɪn}}{{v. 达到； attain；获得}}{{She attained the highest score in the exam.}}
{{attempt}}{{/əˈtempt}}{{v./n. 尝试； attempt}}{{He attempted to climb the mountain.}}
{{attribute}}{{/əˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v./n. 归因于； attribute；属性}}{{She attributed her success to hard work.}}
{{audit}}{{/ˈɔːdɪt}}{{v./n. 审计； audit；旁听}}{{The company's accounts were audited by an external firm.}}
{{authority}}{{/ɔːˈθɒrəti}}{{n. 权威； authority；当局}}{{The local authority approved the construction project.}}
{{automatic}}{{/ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk}}{{adj. 自动的； automatic}}{{The door has an automatic locking system.}}
{{available}}{{/əˈveɪləbl}}{{adj. 可用的； available；有空的}}{{The report is available on the company website.}}
{{aware}}{{/əˈweər}}{{adj. 意识到的； aware}}{{Are you aware of the risks involved?}}
{{barely}}{{/ˈbeəli}}{{adv. 仅仅； barely；几乎不}}{{He barely passed the exam.}}
{{barrier}}{{/ˈbæriər}}{{n. 障碍； barrier；屏障}}{{Language can be a barrier to communication.}}
{{basis}}{{/ˈbeɪsɪs}}{{n. 基础； basis；根据}}{{The theory has no scientific basis.}}
{{behalf}}{{/bɪˈhɑːf}}{{n. 代表； on behalf of}}{{I am writing on behalf of the committee.}}
{{benefit}}{{/ˈbenɪfɪt}}{{n./v. 好处； benefit；受益}}{{Regular exercise has many health benefits.}}
{{bias}}{{/ˈbaɪəs}}{{n./v. 偏见； bias；偏向}}{{The report was criticized for its political bias.}}
{{bind}}{{/baɪnd}}{{v. 约束； bind；捆绑}}{{The contract binds both parties to the agreement.}}
{{blame}}{{/bleɪm}}{{v./n. 责备； blame；归咎于}}{{Nobody was to blame for the accident.}}
{{blast}}{{/blɑːst}}{{n./v. 爆炸； blast；冲击波}}{{The blast destroyed several buildings.}}
{{blend}}{{/blend}}{{v./n. 混合； blend；融合}}{{The coffee is a blend of several different beans.}}
{{block}}{{/blɒk}}{{v./n. 阻挡； block；街区}}{{A fallen tree blocked the road.}}
{{boom}}{{/buːm}}{{n./v. 繁荣； boom；激增}}{{The tech industry experienced a boom in the 2000s.}}
{{boost}}{{/buːst}}{{v./n. 促进； boost；增长}}{{The tax cut will boost consumer spending.}}
{{bound}}{{/baʊnd}}{{adj./v./n. 一定的； bound；界限}}{{She is bound to succeed with her talent.}}
{{breach}}{{/briːtʃ}}{{n./v. 违反； breach；缺口}}{{The company was in breach of the contract.}}
{{brief}}{{/briːf}}{{adj./n./v. 简短的； brief；简报}}{{The manager gave a brief overview of the project.}}
{{brilliant}}{{/ˈbrɪliənt}}{{adj. 杰出的； brilliant；灿烂的}}{{She is a brilliant scientist.}}
{{broad}}{{/brɔːd}}{{adj. 广泛的； broad；宽阔的}}{{The course covers a broad range of topics.}}
{{budget}}{{/ˈbʌdʒɪt}}{{n./v. 预算； budget；编预算}}{{The government increased the education budget.}}
{{bulk}}{{/bʌlk}}{{n. 大部分； bulk；体积}}{{The bulk of the work has been completed.}}
{{burden}}{{/ˈbɜːdn}}{{n./v. 负担； burden；使负重}}{{The tax burden on small businesses is heavy.}}
{{bureau}}{{/ˈbjʊərəʊ}}{{n. 局； bureau；办公室}}{{The Federal Bureau of Investigation handles the case.}}
{{campaign}}{{/kæmˈpeɪn}}{{n./v. 运动； campaign；竞选活动}}{{The charity launched a campaign to raise awareness.}}
{{candidate}}{{/ˈkændɪdət}}{{n. 候选人； candidate；应试者}}{{There are three candidates for the position.}}
{{capable}}{{/ˈkeɪpəbl}}{{adj. 有能力的； capable}}{{She is capable of handling the task.}}
{{capacity}}{{/kəˈpæsəti}}{{n. 容量； capacity；能力}}{{The stadium has a capacity of 50,000 people.}}
{{capture}}{{/ˈkæptʃər}}{{v./n. 捕获； capture；夺取}}{{The photographer captured the moment perfectly.}}
{{cast}}{{/kɑːst}}{{v./n. 投； cast；演员阵容}}{{She cast a glance at her watch.}}
{{casual}}{{/ˈkæʒuəl}}{{adj. 随意的； casual；非正式的}}{{He was wearing casual clothes.}}
{{category}}{{/ˈkætəɡəri}}{{n. 类别； category}}{{The products are divided into several categories.}}
{{cease}}{{/siːs}}{{v. 停止； cease}}{{The factory ceased production last month.}}
{{champion}}{{/ˈtʃæmpiən}}{{n./v. 冠军； champion；拥护}}{{She has always championed the cause of education.}}
{{channel}}{{/ˈtʃænl}}{{n./v. 渠道； channel；引导}}{{The company uses various channels to reach customers.}}
{{chapter}}{{/ˈtʃæptər}}{{n. 章节； chapter；阶段}}{{Please read Chapter 5 before the next class.}}
{{charter}}{{/ˈtʃɑːtər}}{{n./v. 宪章； charter；包租}}{{The United Nations Charter promotes international peace.}}
{{chronic}}{{/ˈkrɒnɪk}}{{adj. 慢性的； chronic；长期的}}{{He suffers from chronic back pain.}}
{{circulate}}{{/ˈsɜːkjuleɪt}}{{v. 循环； circulate；传播}}{{The rumor circulated quickly through the office.}}
{{circumstance}}{{/ˈsɜːkəmstəns}}{{n. 环境； circumstance；情况}}{{Under the circumstances, the decision was reasonable.}}
{{cite}}{{/saɪt}}{{v. 引用； cite；举例}}{{She cited several studies to support her argument.}}
{{civil}}{{/ˈsɪvl}}{{adj. 公民的； civil；文明的}}{{Civil rights are protected by law.}}
{{claim}}{{/kleɪm}}{{v./n. 声称； claim；索赔}}{{He claims to have seen the accident.}}
{{clarify}}{{/ˈklærɪfaɪ}}{{v. 澄清； clarify；阐明}}{{Could you clarify what you mean?}}
{{classify}}{{/ˈklæsɪfaɪ}}{{v. 分类； classify；归类}}{{The documents were classified as top secret.}}
{{climate}}{{/ˈklaɪmət}}{{n. 气候； climate；风气}}{{Climate change is a global concern.}}
{{cling}}{{/klɪŋ}}{{v. 紧握； cling；坚持}}{{The child clung to her mother's hand.}}
{{coincide}}{{/ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd}}{{v. 巧合； coincide；同时发生}}{{The two events coincided by chance.}}
{{collapse}}{{/kəˈlæps}}{{v./n. 倒塌； collapse；崩溃}}{{The building collapsed during the earthquake.}}
{{colleague}}{{/ˈkɒliːɡ}}{{n. 同事； colleague}}{{She discussed the project with her colleagues.}}
{{combine}}{{/kəmˈbaɪn}}{{v. 结合； combine；联合}}{{The hotel combines luxury with comfort.}}
{{command}}{{/kəˈmɑːnd}}{{v./n. 命令； command；掌握}}{{The general commanded his troops to advance.}}
{{comment}}{{/ˈkɒment}}{{n./v. 评论； comment}}{{She made a comment about the weather.}}
{{commission}}{{/kəˈmɪʃn}}{{n./v. 委员会； commission；委托}}{{The government set up a commission to investigate the issue.}}
{{commit}}{{/kəˈmɪt}}{{v. 承诺； commit；犯（错误）}}{{The company committed resources to the project.}}
{{commodity}}{{/kəˈmɒdəti}}{{n. 商品； commodity}}{{Oil is a valuable commodity.}}
{{communicate}}{{/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt}}{{v. 交流； communicate；传达}}{{It is important to communicate effectively with your team.}}
{{community}}{{/kəˈmjuːnəti}}{{n. 社区； community；群体}}{{The local community organized a fundraiser.}}
{{compact}}{{/kəmˈpækt}}{{adj./n. 紧凑的； compact；协议}}{{The car is compact and easy to park.}}
{{comparable}}{{/ˈkɒmpərəbl}}{{adj. 可比的； comparable；类似的}}{{The two products are comparable in quality.}}
{{comparison}}{{/kəmˈpærɪsn}}{{n. 比较； comparison}}{{In comparison with last year, sales have increased.}}
{{compatible}}{{/kəmˈpætəbl}}{{adj. 兼容的； compatible；和谐的}}{{The new software is compatible with most computers.}}
{{compel}}{{/kəmˈpel}}{{v. 迫使； compel；强迫}}{{The evidence compelled him to change his mind.}}
{{compensate}}{{/ˈkɒmpenseɪt}}{{v. 补偿； compensate；酬报}}{{The company compensated the workers for their overtime.}}
{{compile}}{{/kəmˈpaɪl}}{{v. 编译； compile；汇编}}{{She compiled a list of useful resources.}}
{{complain}}{{/kəmˈpleɪn}}{{v. 抱怨； complain；投诉}}{{Customers complained about the poor service.}}
{{complement}}{{/ˈkɒmplɪment}}{{v./n. 补充； complement；补语}}{{The wine complements the meal perfectly.}}
{{complex}}{{/ˈkɒmpleks}}{{adj./n. 复杂的； complex；综合体}}{{The issue is more complex than it appears.}}
{{comply}}{{/kəmˈplaɪ}}{{v. 遵守； comply；服从}}{{All companies must comply with the regulations.}}
{{component}}{{/kəmˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 成分； component；部件}}{{Each component of the machine must be inspected.}}
{{compose}}{{/kəmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 组成； compose；作曲}}{{The committee is composed of ten members.}}
{{comprehensive}}{{/ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv}}{{adj. 全面的； comprehensive；综合的}}{{The report provides a comprehensive analysis of the issue.}}
{{compromise}}{{/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz}}{{n./v. 妥协； compromise；折中}}{{Both sides reached a compromise.}}
{{compulsory}}{{/kəmˈpʌlsəri}}{{adj. 强制的； compulsory；必修的}}{{Education is compulsory for children aged 5 to 16.}}
{{conceive}}{{/kənˈsiːv}}{{v. 构想； conceive；怀孕}}{{She conceived a plan to improve efficiency.}}
{{concentrate}}{{/ˈkɒnsntreɪt}}{{v. 集中； concentrate；专注}}{{I need to concentrate on my studies.}}
{{concept}}{{/ˈkɒnsept}}{{n. 概念； concept；观念}}{{The concept of freedom is central to democracy.}}
{{conclude}}{{/kənˈkluːd}}{{v. 结束； conclude；得出结论}}{{The study concluded that exercise improves mental health.}}
{{concrete}}{{/ˈkɒŋkriːt}}{{adj./n. 具体的； concrete；混凝土}}{{We need concrete evidence, not just theories.}}
{{condemn}}{{/kənˈdem}}{{v. 谴责； condemn；判刑}}{{The government condemned the terrorist attack.}}
{{conduct}}{{/kənˈdʌkt}}{{v./n. 进行； conduct；行为}}{{The researchers conducted a series of experiments.}}
{{conference}}{{/ˈkɒnfərəns}}{{n. 会议； conference；讨论}}{{The annual conference will be held in Beijing.}}
{{confine}}{{/kənˈfaɪn}}{{v. 限制； confine； confinement}}{{The discussion was confined to the main topic.}}
{{confirm}}{{/kənˈfɜːm}}{{v. 确认； confirm；证实}}{{Please confirm your reservation by email.}}
{{conflict}}{{/ˈkɒnflɪkt}}{{n./v. 冲突； conflict；矛盾}}{{There is a conflict between the two departments.}}
